Turn a scanned book into Markdown
	:comment Challenge: OCR scrambles vertical text
	:comment Approach: let Vision recover the order
	Start the run@$ vbook book.pdf -o out
	:while Pages left?
		Render the page at --dpi@(never past the scan's own pixels)
		Recognize the document structure@(serialized: Vision crashes@ when run concurrently)
		:if Figures wanted?
			Remove recognized text from the ink
			Crop the remaining ink as PNG
			Drop text that falls inside a figure
		:else
			Skip figures (--no-figures)
		Sort blocks into reading order
			:if Most lines run top to bottom?
				Columns right to left
			:else
				Top to bottom
	Write <title>.md and <title>_images/
	:terminal Markdown plus figure images
